{"id":"dag","ord":"a0","title":"DAG","desc":"Workflow TEMPLATES — the pipeline a lane walks, defined ONCE as a subtree: each step a `todo` node, dependencies as `after` edges. The app draws blocked-vs-ready, so the template is its own diagram, and `set_doing` refusing on a blocked node makes the order a refusal rather than a discipline. LAW: never mark anything here — dispatch CLONES a template under a new lane node in lanes.olai (real copies via `add_node`, one call with `children`), then rewrites the `after` edges onto the clone's ids with `set_after` (capture children cannot carry edges yet — the one wrinkle this prototype surfaced). Step ids are `dag-<template>-<step>`; a clone keeps the `<step>` suffixes under a `lane-<task>-` prefix, so mark-flipping needs no search. EDGE RULE the template must encode: a step that MUTATES the worktree sits `after` every step that READS it — readers fan out, writers wait.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr","parent":"dag","ord":"a0","title":"pr — implement through merge","desc":"The default pipeline for a dispatched PR lane. Facts the clone carries as properties: `agent`/`repo`/`item` on the lane node, `terminal` on implement, `pr` on the step that opened it.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-implement","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a0","title":"implement + open PR","todo":true,"desc":"Dispatch IS `set_doing` here. The clone's copy carries `terminal` as a property; `pr` lands when the PR opens.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-refactor","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a1","title":"refactor passes","todo":true,"desc":"Only for a non-trivial, non-test-only code change — otherwise SKIPPED. The author refactors its own PR, pushing each step as an isolated commit, per the orchestrator instructions: architecture-first-principles; hickey and lowy TOGETHER, with human intuition keeping the architecture simple; /simplify when the author is Claude. The instructions list these as method, not as ordered sub-steps — one step here, deliberately.","after":["dag-pr-implement"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-15T19:05:50-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-review-grok","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a2","title":"review: grok","todo":true,"desc":"Reader of the worktree — fans out with the other review the moment refactor is done. SPAWN SHAPE (the charter's rule, enforced by the human 2026-08-16): a reviewer opens as a SPLIT of the author's terminal — kolu create --parent &lt;author-terminal&gt; --cwd &lt;worktree&gt; — never as a top-level terminal.","after":["dag-pr-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-16T14:14:55-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-review-opencode","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a3","title":"review: opencode","todo":true,"desc":"Same spawn shape as the grok review: a SPLIT of the author's terminal (kolu create --parent &lt;author-terminal&gt; --cwd &lt;worktree&gt;), per the charter, enforced by the human 2026-08-16.","after":["dag-pr-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-16T14:14:55-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-merge-master","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a4","title":"merge latest master into the PR","todo":true,"desc":"A MERGE COMMIT, never a rebase (ruled 2026-08-15: faster, and history stays put). Per CLAUDE.md this step runs ONLY when the PR has conflicts or CI needs code from master — otherwise it is SKIPPED, same pattern as the deferral gate. WRITER: sits after both reviews because it mutates the worktree they read — the 2026-08-15 rebase-under-live-reviewers incident is why this edge exists.","after":["dag-pr-review-grok","dag-pr-review-opencode"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-15T19:05:52-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-address","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a5","title":"address findings","todo":true,"after":["dag-pr-review-grok","dag-pr-review-opencode"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-15T19:05:52-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-ci","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a6","title":"CI green at head","todo":true,"after":["dag-pr-merge-master","dag-pr-address"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-15T19:05:53-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-evidence","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a7","title":"evidence verified","todo":true,"after":["dag-pr-ci"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-15T19:05:54-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-deferrals","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a8","title":"deferrals ruled #human","todo":true,"desc":"HUMAN gate: a PR whose report carries deferrals merges only on the human's explicit word — each deferral becomes a roadmap node first. A report that says \"no deferrals\" in so many words skips this gate.","after":["dag-pr-evidence"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-15T19:05:55-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-merge","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a9","title":"merge","todo":true,"after":["dag-pr-deferrals"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-15T19:05:55-04:00"}
